<title>RUSSIA: Rouble pressured by funds coming from T-bills.</title>
<headline>Rouble pressured by funds coming from T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The rouble eased in calm trading on Friday and dealers said it was under pressure from funds from the T-bill market, dealers said.</p>
<p> roubles/dollar	Feb 28 midday  Feb 28 early   Feb 27 close</p>
<p> today settlement    5,682-84	 5,680-82	 5,677-79</p>
<p> tomorrow settlement 5,684-85	 5,682-84	 5,680-82</p>
<p> overnight credit (%)    5-10	     5-15	     5-10</p>
<p>			   Feb 28				Feb 27</p>
<p> central bank	  5,671/87			    5,668/84</p>
<p> MICEX		   5,676				 5,674</p>
<p>&quot;The dollar firmed because overnight credits are cheap. Some funds have come back from the T-bill market after (Wednesday's) auctions,&quot; one dealer said.</p>
<p>But dealers said there was little dollar buying on the last day of month because banks are not interested in keeping long positions until next month.</p>
<p>--Artyom Danielyan, Moscow newsroom (095) 941 8520</p>
</text>
